{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"anchor":"Reference","generated":true}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The four rules","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-four-rules"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Drag","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"text":" (helper)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Pure value patch → computed property","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Drag"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"role":"symbol","title":"Interaction","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swami","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"title":"Beats","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"}}}